{
  "rationale": "The plant separates perception (obstacle events) and motion (controllable actions). The specification binds perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery only when needed and prioritizing forward exploration. Helper states manage recovery and last-resort full rotation. All transitions are deterministic and respect the event and state constraints.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model perception and motion as separate plant automata: one for sensing, one for actuation.",
    "Specification automata bind perception states to safe, progress-maximizing actions, enforce conservative recovery, and prevent unsafe or oscillatory behaviors."
  ],
